course: dictionary
lesson: 6976
title: A word with a wide view
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A panorama is a wide view. When you stand on a hill and see the whole valley from side to side, you are looking at a panorama. Context helps here: the words around it, like hill, valley or wide, give you the clue.
explain: Look for capital letters too. «In 1957 the BBC programme Panorama showed a spoof film of spaghetti growing on trees.» The capital P shows that Panorama is the name of a TV programme, not a view. A capital letter is another clue, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Panorama can mean a wide view, a wide photo, or a full overview of a topic, such as «a panorama of history». Ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then swap your meaning in and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A panorama is a wide view of a large area of land, sea or sky.
fact: A panorama can also be a wide photograph that shows a whole scene from side to side.
fact: «Panorama» can mean a full overview of a topic, as in «a panorama of history».
fact: The adjective is panoramic, as in «a panoramic view of the mountains».
fact: Panorama is also the name of a BBC TV programme, so a capital P can show a name.
exercise: The hikers reached the top of the hill and saw a panorama of the valley. What does panorama mean? | A path through the woods | A loud noise from far away | *A wide view of a large area | A small box with a lid
exercise: In «the BBC programme Panorama», what does Panorama mean? | A very old map | A wide view of a scene | *The name of a TV programme | A kind of spaghetti
exercise: Ella's phone has a panorama mode. What does it do? | Turns the phone off | Makes the screen bigger | Plays music | *Takes a wide photo by turning slowly
test: «From the tower we saw a panorama of the whole town.» Which word means nearly the same as panorama here? | Tower | *View | Shadow | Whisper
test: A writer describes a scene in a wide, sweeping way. Which word is the adjective from panorama? | *Panoramic | Painful | Pancake | Panorama-ish
exam: A history book gives a panorama of the 1900s. What does panorama mean here? | A dark, narrow cellar | *A full overview of the period | A loud bang in the street | A small photo of one person
